WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.053 --> 00:00:01.470
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
It's officially

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:04.320
week nine of Google
Cloud Next OnAir, which

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.830
means we're focusing on
business application platform.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:10.530
I'm Priyanka, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:14.160
where we're taking a sneak
peek at this week's content.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.650
Week nine is all about the
business application platform,

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:21.340
meaning we wanted to help
your business be productive.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.730
So we've got a content
lineup that focuses on

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:26.850
how to innovate with
an API-first approach,

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:30.360
as well as how employees can
create apps without coding.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.159
Be sure to explore
the session catalog

00:00:32.159 --> 00:00:34.380
for interesting advice
that could simplify

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.480
your own day-to-day work.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:40.140
Our final spotlight is shining
on this authentication talk,

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.560
which breaks down the many
options and considerations

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.570
that your enterprise faces.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:47.910
From understanding
the basic differences

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:51.420
to identifying what factors
matter most to your company,

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:54.930
this session is sure to
answer some of your questions.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:58.440
My pick of the week is unlocking
the power of your existing

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:01.800
data through APIs because
it addresses a challenge

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:04.230
that we all end up
facing, eventually-

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.960
what to do with the
information that's locked away

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:10.740
in legacy systems or on paper.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:13.680
It's really interesting to
see all of the solutions

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.290
that are available and how
different products approach

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:19.380
the same problem with
a unique perspective.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.330
If you're like me,
then be sure to add

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:23.310
this one to your playlist.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:27.630
Finally, be sure to check out
this video demo of AppSheets,

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:30.510
a tool that enables
employees to create

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:34.620
their own applications without
needing to write any code.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:37.560
Even pro engineers like
tools that are easy to use,

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.050
and AppSheet packs a
lot of the features

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:42.930
into a deceptively
simple package.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:45.450
To add these sessions to
your digital playlist,

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:46.840
check out the link.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.220
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:50.820
Leave us a comment or
tweet us using the hashtag

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:52.230
#GoogleCloudNext.

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:54.920
We'll see you in the cloud.

